quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  8,1,(Esteemed Messenger!) They ask you about (the distribution of) the spoils of war. Say: ‘The spoils belong to Allah and the Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him). So be conscious of Allah and settle the matters (of disagreement) nicely among yourselves. And obey Allah and His Messenger (blessings and peace be upon him) if you are (true) believers.’
  8,2,"The believers are only those who, when Allah is mentioned, their hearts tremble (with reverence). And when His revelations are recited to them, they increase their faith—and they trust in their Lord."
  8,3,(They are those) who establish the prayer and spend out of what We have provided them (in charity).
  8,4,"They are the ones who are the true believers. They shall have (high) ranks in the presence of their Lord, forgiveness and generous provision."
  8,5,"(Esteemed Prophet!) For it was your Lord Who brought you out from your home for a just cause, though a group of the believers were indeed reluctant."
  8,6,They disputed with you about the just cause even after it became clear (to them). (It was) as if they were being driven towards death while they could see themselves.
  8,7,"And (remember) when Allah promised you (victory over) one of the two (enemy) groups, (saying:) ‘It is for you.’ You wished the unarmed one to be yours (for that was easy to encounter). But Allah desired to establish the truth through His Words and to cut off the roots of the (invading) disbelievers,"
  8,8,"so that He may establish the truth (firmly) and nullify falsehood, though the guilty might dislike it."
